--TEST--
an enum a class declares carries its `///` run on the member, and hovering its name in a type answers the enum's name with its owner and then that run, `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;
class Order {
    /// Where an order is on its way to the customer.
    enum Status { Draft, Paid }
}

class Receipt {
    public function show(Order::Sta<|>tus $s): void {
        echo $s;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
enum Shop\Order::Status
```

Where an order is on its way to the customer.
